	(text_box "The SBU1 and SBU2 pins on a USB-C connector are Sideband Use (SBU) pins. They are part of the USB-C standard and serve specialized roles depending on the application, primarily in Alternate Modes (e.g., DisplayPort, Thunderbolt) and certain USB-C accessories.\n\nFor basic USB 2.0/3.0 operation (like in your ESP32-C3-02 design), the SBU pins are not used and can be left unconnected or handled with optional protective measures."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 106.045 42.545 0)
		(size 53.34 25.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2bc9e9b-9954-4180-be55-d5f34b96185f")
	)
	(text_box "USB-C allows for reversible cable insertion. Both pairs of data pins (DP1/DN1 and DP2/DN2) are electrically identical but physically flipped depending on the cable orientation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
